adjudication.rationale:
In `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the auth check is:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403)
}
```

If `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is not set in the environment (i.e., `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is `undefined`) and the request omits the header (so the header lookup also yields `undefined`), then the comparison is `undefined !== undefined`, which is `false`, so the request is accepted. The endpoint then decrypts and upserts credentials for an arbitrary `userId` from the body, so this becomes an authentication bypass when the secret is unset.

Additionally, Node/Next normalizes incoming header keys to lowercase in `req.headers`; if `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME` contains uppercase letters, the lookup may miss the actual header value (returning `undefined`). With a properly set secret this causes denial (403), but combined with an unset secret it also contributes to the same bypass described above.
